      "dom_id": "question-36111",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+12y-z+13=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $y$ term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+12y-z+13 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3({y}^{2}+4y)-z+13 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3[(y+2)^{2}-4]-z+13 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y+2)^{2}-12-z+13 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y+2)^{2}-z+1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3(y+2)^{2}-z+1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y+2)^{2} & =z-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic paraboloid centered at $(0,-2,1).$",
