      "problem": "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\nz=1+(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of an elliptic paraboloid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand an elliptic paraboloid centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}},\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an elliptic paraboloid with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,2,1),\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$",
